# SPEC_CHAT_APP C1: the phone's chat app, read only, on 127.0.0.1:8712 only (fixed in router/chat.py, never 0.0.0.0 or
# `localhost`). It holds no key, runs no model and has no route that changes anything. The phone reaches it through
# an SSH local forward (permitopen="127.0.0.1:8712", added by hand to the iphone-viewer key; it is removed again at C4).
# Go-live checklist: (1) update the ~/pilot3a_live checkout to the commit that has router/chat.py (that checkout also runs argus-control and
# the stage proxy, which take the new code at their next restart); (2) add permitopen="127.0.0.1:8712" to the iphone-viewer key by hand;
# (3) open the page once on the phone: the job list shows and the console has no CSP error.
# C2: the issue writer's actions need the key files of the CLI in the service's environment, deliberately and by hand (a drop-in
# like argus-control.service.d): ARGUS_CHAT_KEY_FILE (code jobs) and ARGUS_CHAT_WRITER_KEY_FILE (the writer's turns). Without them
# every paid action is refused at prepare. The service never reads the files.
# Install (after "go live"): ln -s this file into ~/.config/systemd/user/, then
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload && systemctl --user enable --now argus-chat.service
[Unit]
Description=Argus chat app for the phone (127.0.0.1:8712)

[Service]
Type=simple
WorkingDirectory=%h/pilot3a_live
ExecStart=%h/pilot3a_live/.venv-verify/bin/python scripts/argus.py chat serve
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5
NoNewPrivileges=yes

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
